:18631,"title":"","description":"0","card_type":"comments","type":"comments","url":"","style":null,"length":0,"continue_watching_progress":0}],"id":0,"title":"Comments","section_type":"comments"}],"post_info":{"genres":["Action","Drama","Comedy"],"id":18631,"type":"SERIES","title":"Bol Bachchan","logo":"","image":"https://cdn6.albox.co/storage/disk56/seasons/17beb634-755f-4635-849e-6469b6e5ac1d.jpg","background_image":"https://cdn6.albox.co/storage/disk55/seasons/667e3ea9-15f4-437b-a1f2-d490c5e6528d.jpg","likes":36,"dislikes":2,"views":6003,"release_date":"1341532800000","season_number":1,"description":"When a child falls into the well of the temple and Abbas breaks the temple's lock to save the child. When Prithviraj arrives at the scene, Ravi says Abbas's name as Abhishek Bachchan to avoid religious controversies of a temple being broken open by a Muslim. Prithviraj hires Abhishek Bachchan (Abbas) and is happy with his work, but Ravi and his friends have to come up with a new plan when Prithviraj spots Abbas celebrating Eid as a Muslim. Abbas and the others convince Prithviraj that the one celebrating Eid was actually 'Abbas', an effeminate man and classical Kathak dancer. Things become worse for Abbas and Ravi when Prithviraj kindly hires Abbas for teaching Kathak to his sister Radhika (Prachi Desai). The more Abbas tries to manage his dual life without letting Prithviraj know, the more he has to lie to cover up other lies; this forms the crux of the story.","rating":{"sources":[{"title":"IMDb","logo":"https://a7.pnghunt.com/preview/450/662/555/computer-wallpaper-text-brand-yellow-imdb.jpg","max_value":10,"value":5.5}],"value":5.5,"age":"PG-13"},"background_color":"","current_season_id":6974,"content_control":"NORMAL"}}